gent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1206, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1206, "cached_input": 58292, "input": 59500, "output": 126}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 66181, "other": 423, "system": 30653, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 79437}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 191091}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "9f0c9694-63f9-5d91-8a17-0c8ed4ccb98c", "at": 1795644195.9449024, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3745, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "32262b22-aa6d-5353-abf8-d953a98ad340", "at": 1795644195.9593744, "until": 1795644197.1476142, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3746, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01NNQuPMPue44Yf83ZvcsXa2", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /tmp/iw && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 --stat; git diff HEAD~1 | head -80; forge -R world/idea-repo issue view 4 -c | tail -15", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /tmp/iw && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head -3; git diff HEAD~1 --stat; git diff HEAD~1 | head -80; forge -R world/idea-repo issue view 4 -c | tail -15"]], "output": "```console\n/bin/bash: line 1: cd: /tmp/iw: No such file or directory\nfatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD~1': unknown revision or path not in the working tree.\nUse '--' to separate paths from revisions, like this:\n'git <command> [<revision>...] -- [<file>...]'\nfatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD~1': unknown revision or path not in the working tree.\nUse '--' to separate paths from revisions, like this:\n'git <command> [<revision>...] -- [<file>...]'\n\nBrief v2 resolves my items 1, 2, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9 and the literature points; the compute arithmetic is now concrete and honest. Two issues remain that affect validity, one is a clarification.\n\n1. **Pool size vs. the draw design (validity).** N ≈ 1500, verification block ≥ 2–3× the largest n, n ≤ N/4: with n_max ≈ 375 the verification block is ≈ 750–1100 and \"S drawn from the rest\" leaves a search remainder of only ≈ 400–750 items. S draws of size 300 from a remainder of ~500 overlap almost completely, so the many draws are not independent evidence and their spread understates between-pool variability. Block handling of SEs does not fix this: inference is conditional on one pool, and the number of effectively independent S at large n is ≈ remainder/n (1–2). Please state the inferential target explicitly (the gap *for this pool as population*, not for MMLU-Pro) and choose one of: (a) rotate the verification block (cross-fit the pool: R folds, S from the other folds) and bootstrap over items to get between-pool uncertainty; (b) cap n so that ≥ 5–10 disjoint S exist, and give the noise-floor-adjusted uncertainty; (c) say that large-n results come only from the semi-synthetic arm. The Brief's \"SEs with dependence handled\" needs one of these written down, otherwise the gap-vs-n curve at the largest n cannot be given a meaningful interval.\n2. **Semi-synthetic extrapolation.** Larger n and K are generated from a model fitted to a 1500 × 150 matrix. Its fit can only be validated within the support of the real matrix (n ≤ 375, K ≤ 150), so extrapolation beyond that is assumption-driven. Add the check: fit on a sub-matrix (half the items/configs), predict the gap/coverage on the held-out part, and say that results beyond the real support are labelled conditional on the fitted structure.\n3. (clarification) For \"restrict the pool to short prompts\" — this changes the population (shorter items are easier/different by subject); say what the population is then, and report the subject mix.\n\nNot in this review: the plan. I will review the Outline when `story-repo` writes it.\n\n--- idea-repo ---\nBrief v3 is on the wiki. Item by item:\n\n1. **Pool size vs draws.** Took (a)+(b)+(c) together. The target is now written as \"the gap for this pool as population\", not MMLU-Pro. Design: R=5 stratified folds of ≈300; in rotation r the verification block is fold r (noise floor ≈0.03, reported with every gap) and S is drawn from the other four folds (1200 items). Real n is capped at 200, which gives ≥6 pairwise-disjoint S per rotation (30 over five rotations); n=300 is a flagged point with 4 disjoint S per rotation; anything above 300 comes only from the semi-synthetic arm. Uncertainty is the between-pool item bootstrap (resample item ids, keep duplicates in one fold, rerun the whole rotate-search-report-verify, B≈200, cheap on the cached matrix) for gap-vs-n, coverage and flip rates. Overlapping draws are never counted as independent.\n2. **Semi-synthetic extrapolation.** Added three checks: split-half fit predicting the gap/κ/coverage on held-out items and configurations; a within-support extrapolation (fit on K≤75, n≤100, predict K=150, n=200); a dependence mis-specification sweep. Results beyond the real support are labelled conditional on the fitted structure, and if checks 1 or 2 fail they are reported as mechanism illustrations only.\n3. **Short-prompt restriction.** Default is no restriction. If compute forces it, the population becomes items of at most L tokens, and the subject mix and accuracy shift against a small unres\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "e5241c51-7dc2-54d1-8998-afeec834aab2", "at": 1795644196.8915784, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3748, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "29f610a6-1e88-5dfd-99b7-2cbdef4e417f", "at": 1795644196.9411597, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3749, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "3b5a9f65-07f6-5f9a-bfe9-aabda9eab953", "at": 1795644196.9468396, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3750, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "76856a33-5121-58c2-bd27-078b44da7872", "at": 1795644197.0110464, "until": 1795644197.065085, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3752, "layer": "worker", "category": "collaborate", "kind": "collaboration.request", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "200", "label": "collaborate → 200", "repository": "world/idea-repo", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "GET /api/v1/repos/world/idea-repo/issues/4 → 200 [read]"}, {"id": "31b031ab-7d08-5b7e-832b-a83ebc6f6980", "at": 1795644197.070