equence": 3813, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "639c7e0a-2b69-5b37-9545-e10a638834e2", "at": 1795644207.17498, "until": 1795644207.9074795, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3814, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "ef64aac4d58834e6ac2b5cedc28cf07e", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (67 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "I read Brief v3 and it answers review 2 (`idea-repo`#4, now closed). I'm asking `idea-repo` for nothing further.\n\n- **Pool as population:** the Brief now states that the gap is for this pool, not for MMLU-Pro. It rotates five verification folds, caps n at 200 so at least six disjoint search sets exist per rotation, and bootstraps over items.\n- **Semi-synthetic extrapolation:** it adds checks on held-out items and configurations. Results beyond the real range are labelled as conditional.\n- **Short-prompt restriction:** the default is now no restriction. If compute forces one, the Brief reports the subject mix and scopes every claim to that population.\n\nOne residual note, which I recorded in `idea-review-repo`#2 and didn't send to the owner. The verification noise per rotation is about 3 points, which is comparable to the expected gap. Per-draw coverage and flip results therefore rest on the pooled rotations and the bootstrap.\n\nThe plan review still waits for the Outline from `story-repo`."}}, {"id": "c916ec7c-695b-513c-9e70-c1ca3781cd4a", "at": 1795644207.9098368, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3882, "layer": "worker"